Package: multilpa
Title: Two-Level Latent Profile Analysis
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mohammed", "Saqr", , "saqr@saqr.me", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5881-3109")),
    person("Sonsoles", "L\u00f3pez-Pernas", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9621-1392")))
Description: Fits two-level latent profile and latent class models using a
    nested expectation-maximization algorithm. Indicators may be continuous,
    categorical, or a mixture of the two. Individual profiles share measurement
    parameters across discrete group classes, which differ in their profile
    proportions. Supports observed-data likelihood
    for missing indicators, diagonal or full residual covariance, observed
    information and robust sandwich inference, class-membership covariates,
    class enumeration, and parametric bootstrap comparisons. Latent transition
    models estimate first-order transition probabilities between profiles over ordered
    occasions, optionally varying across group classes, by a forward-backward
    expectation-maximization algorithm. Includes multiple starts, posterior
    classification, explicit variance constraints, tidy accessors, information
    criteria under both multilevel sample-size conventions, classification
    quality diagnostics, and entropy summaries.
    The nonparametric multilevel mixture formulation follows Vermunt (2003)
    <doi:10.1111/j.0081-1750.2003.t01-1-00131.x>.
